From 8d545d7be893c5ac75687fc798286cda4599e1e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:48:45 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] zed, install_cli, title_bar: "Install CLI" only while zeo is
 not reachable
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Zeo next proposal §6.25. The app menu showed "Install CLI" always, and
on Linux it installed nothing: it opened a prompt saying the CLI
"should already be installed", in Zed's words, naming zeditor and
zedit. Both packages (app-editors/zeo, zeo-bin) put the command at
/usr/bin/zeo, so on a packaged install the item was always noise.

At startup, before the menus are first built, CliPresence looks for an
executable `zeo` in the PATH's absolute directories and then in
~/.local/bin, which a desktop session's PATH often lacks. A relative
PATH entry is skipped: it resolves against whatever directory the
editor started in, which is not the command a shell would run. The
lookup is synchronous on purpose -- a handful of stat calls -- because
the menus read the answer right after it; a background lookup would
build them once with the stale item. Found, app_menus drops the item,
matched by its action rather than its label. Only a file can be seen:
a shell `alias zeo=…` lives in an rc file, not in the GUI's
environment, and is not detected.

On Linux the item now does something: it links ~/.local/bin/zeo to the
command beside the editor in the release layout (<prefix>/libexec/
zeo-editor, <prefix>/bin/zeo), with no root. A file already there is
left alone unless it is that same link -- it may be the operator's own
wrapper. On success the menus are rebuilt without the item and a toast
says where the link is, adding a PATH hint when ~/.local/bin is not on
it; on failure a prompt says why and that a package installs
/usr/bin/zeo. macOS keeps upstream's flow and Windows has no item.

The title bar's application menu (Linux) holds a copy of the menus
taken when it was built, and re-read them only when disable_ai
changed, so set_menus alone left the item on screen. It now also
observes CliPresence. That makes title_bar depend on install_cli; the
three Cargo.lock lines are the new edges and nothing else.

Logs: one JSON line at startup (cli_presence, with the path found)
and one per install attempt (cli_linked / cli_link_failed).

Tests: install_cli cli_presence::tests (found on the PATH; a symlink in
~/.local/bin found off the PATH; a non-executable file, a dangling
link, a directory and another name are not; a relative PATH entry is
not; the link is made, found and idempotent; an existing file is left
alone; no link when no command sits beside the editor; marking
installed rebuilds the menus once). zed::app_menus::cli_tests (the
item shows with no lookup and when not found, goes when found; it is
dropped from a submenu without its neighbours). title_bar
test_entries_refresh_when_cli_presence_changes. Seen failing with
drop_install_cli a no-op, the title bar's observer not rebuilding, and
find_cli neither adding ~/.local/bin nor skipping relative entries.
---

